---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · Shift" description="How Shift, a Gmail app for macOS, accesses, uses, stores and shares your data." path="/privacy">
  <main id="main" class="wrap doc">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 24 November 2026</p>

    <p>Shift is an email app for macOS that works with Gmail. It is made by TALKK ("we"), a web and app studio in Byron Bay, Australia. This policy explains what Shift does with your information, including the data it receives from your Google account.</p>

    <p class="note">The short version: Shift runs on your Mac and talks directly to Google. We run no servers for it, so your email, contacts and sign-in never reach us. Shift collects no analytics and shows no ads.</p>

    <h2>The Google data Shift accesses</h2>
    <p>When you add a Google account, Shift asks Google for permission to read, send, change and delete your Gmail mail (the scope <code>https://mail.google.com/</code>). It uses that permission for these features and nothing else:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Reading:</strong> your messages, threads, labels, attachments and drafts, to show your mailboxes and conversations.</li>
      <li><strong>Sending and drafts:</strong> sending the emails you write, saving drafts and sending scheduled emails at the time you chose.</li>
      <li><strong>Organising:</strong> archiving, labelling, starring, marking read or unread, moving to Spam or Trash, and creating, renaming, recolouring or deleting labels when you ask it to.</li>
      <li><strong>Permanent deletion:</strong> emptying your Trash or Spam folder when you choose Empty Trash or Empty Spam. This is the reason Shift needs full mail access rather than a narrower permission.</li>
      <li><strong>Your email address,</strong> to tell your accounts apart.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where your data is kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your mail</strong> is copied into a database on your Mac (in Shift's folder under Application Support), so the app works quickly and offline. It stays there until you remove the account.</li>
      <li><strong>Your sign-in</strong> (the token Google issues to Shift) is stored in the macOS Keychain, never in a file and never on a server.</li>
      <li><strong>Attachments you open</strong> are saved to your Downloads folder.</li>
      <li><strong>Your settings,</strong> such as signatures and shortcuts, are saved in a file on your Mac.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who your data is shared with</h2>
    <p>We don't receive, sell or share your data, and we don't use it for advertising or to train AI models. Shift only connects to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google,</strong> to read and change your mail through the Gmail API, and to sign you in.</li>
      <li><strong>Google's public icon service,</strong> to show company logos next to senders. Shift sends only the sender's web domain (for example, <code>example.com</code>), never your messages or your address.</li>
      <li><strong>Senders' image servers,</strong> but only after you choose Load images on an email (or turn on Load remote images in Settings). Those servers then see that the email was opened, which is why images are hidden by default.</li>
      <li><strong>Links you click,</strong> which open in your web browser.</li>
      <li><strong>The AI provider you choose,</strong> only if you set one up in Settings → AI (see below).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>Shift's AI features are off until you add your own account with an AI provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, xAI, Mistral, OpenRouter, a local Ollama server or another compatible service) in Settings → AI. Shift then sends that provider only what the feature you use needs, directly from your Mac, under your account and that provider's terms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Write with AI</strong> sends the text you ask it to rewrite.</li>
      <li><strong>Draft a reply</strong> sends the conversation you're replying to and any notes you've typed.</li>
      <li><strong>Auto-label</strong>, if you turn it on, sends the sender, subject and preview of new Inbox mail, with the label descriptions you wrote. Label my Inbox now sends the same for your newest Inbox emails.</li>
      <li><strong>Clean up Inbox</strong> sends the sender, subject and preview of your newest Inbox emails when you open it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We never see any of it. Your API key stays in the macOS Keychain. Check your provider's terms for how it keeps and uses requests: paid API plans generally don't train on them, but some free tiers do.</p>

    <h2>Limited Use</h2>
    <p>Shift's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Specifically, Shift uses Google user data only to provide the email features described above. No person at TALKK reads your data. It is transferred only to the AI provider you choose, only to perform the AI feature you use, and it is never used for advertising or to develop or train AI or machine-learning models.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and tracking</h2>
    <p>Shift contains no analytics, crash reporting, advertising or tracking code. This website sets no cookies.</p>

    <h2>Early access sign-ups</h2>
    <p>If you ask for early access on this website, we keep the email address you enter and the date, so we can tell you about new versions of Shift. We don't share it, sell it or add it to anyone else's list. To have it removed, write to <a href="mailto:hello@getshiftmail.com">hello@getshiftmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Removing your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Signing out of an account in Shift deletes that account's copy of your mail from your Mac and its sign-in from your Keychain.</li>
      <li>To withdraw Shift's access to your Google account, remove it at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.</li>
      <li>Deleting the Shift app and its folder in Application Support removes everything else it stored.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your mail itself stays in Gmail, where Google's own privacy policy applies.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>Shift signs in with Google's standard OAuth flow for desktop apps, so it never sees your Google password. Data travels to Google over encrypted connections. Scripts inside emails are blocked, and attachments you open are marked as downloaded from the internet, so macOS checks them as it would a browser download.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Shift is not directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top. A significant change, such as a new kind of data leaving your Mac, will also be announced in the app before it takes effect.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests about your data: <a href="mailto:hello@getshiftmail.com">hello@getshiftmail.com</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
